  "finish_delivery_chain": [
    "AR engine strategy uses prefill_interval for decode loop_count and extra KV preallocation for upcoming decode steps; prefill itself stays one forward.",
    "Every model step runs sampling and the original stopping criterion. The block loop does not break when a sequence first becomes stopped.",
    "ARSequenceStrategy marks a stopped sequence finished; later outputs for non-RUNNING sequences are ignored.",
    "EngineLoop creates CPU InferOutput(finish=True), puts outputs into resp_queue, and send_response_loop waits on forward_event before _send_resps.",
    "The event is a reference-counted CounterEvent, not merely an independent boolean flag. EngineLoop also clears it at the midpoint of its output loop.",
    "UniExecutor passes the same event to the model agent. Agent input preprocessing clears it, and agent background execution sets it only after the entire decode block returns.",
    "MPExecutor.start ignores the event argument and starts its remote worker without the shared event. Therefore UniExecutor can expose a full-block delivery delay that is absent or differently scheduled with MPExecutor.",
    "After the event opens, _send_resp selects ResponseType.FINISH and EngineInstance yields the final output and breaks. Static ordering does not quantify the observed delay; use timestamps."
  ],
  "semantics": [
    "Changing interval does not directly change weights, activation precision, temperature, top_p, max_new_tokens, min_new_tokens, or stop words.",
    "The stop condition is evaluated each token and later stopped outputs are suppressed, so the intended returned-token contract remains unchanged.",
    "Within a block, sampling random_offsets increments per token. At a new block, offsets are rebuilt from seq.num_valid_ids and the explicitly provided seed. This supports equivalent seeded behavior but is not a substitute for output-identity tests.",
    "Interval also changes KV preallocation and input/scheduling granularity. Exact output identity must be checked, particularly seeded stochastic generation and natural EOS; fixed greedy 18/64 output checks alone do not establish full navigation equivalence."
  ],
  "performance_and_fairness": [
    "Smaller intervals reduce post-stop tail work and the maximum number of remaining forwards before response delivery can resume.",
    "Interval=1 increases scheduler, CPU input rebuilding and small input-transfer frequency; interval=4 may balance these costs against short-output tail delay.",
    "For long output or multi-request serving, a larger interval may improve throughput while increasing admission/response latency. Batch1 findings do not establish a general concurrent-serving optimum.",
    "Compare FP16 and each quantized model at the same executor and interval. Report old-to-new system acceleration separately from quantization speedup under the new matched system.",
    "Do not count an actual-forward reduction as a change in returned-token workload. Report returned tokens, actual forwards, HTTP latency and model-stage time separately.",
    "Treat interval selection as a candidate system setting; freeze it before final paired tests and quality checks."
  ],
  "inprocess_limits": [
    "Native Engine(False) is implemented, but the HTTP entry deliberately forces mp mode. Our guarded bridge overrides that construction choice and is not a public HTTP configuration guarantee.",
    "In-process frontend and model tasks share an event loop. Blocking CPU work, model dispatch or CUDA synchronizations may affect HTTP responsiveness and cancellation; current tests are single concurrent request only.",
    "The ZMQ path wraps ordinary worker method exceptions into RPC error responses. The native path relies on local engine-task exception/cancellation handling; neither source inspection alone proves reliable HTTP error delivery after every GPU failure.",
    "A fatal process-level CUDA/native failure in the in-process engine also takes down the HTTP process. Removing the worker process removes that isolation boundary.",
    "Native Engine.close cancels its main task and releases executor resources in the task finally path; the loop must remain alive long enough to complete cleanup.",
    "The HTTP serve function has no explicit async_engine.close after uvicorn.run, and its lifespan finally only handles metrics. The outer ZMQ engine registers its own atexit close; native Engine has no corresponding registration in these inspected files. Whole-service process exit releases OS-owned resources, but repeated in-process construction/destruction needs explicit cleanup testing.",
    "Do not start fork-based CUDA workers after initializing a CUDA context in the frontend. This candidate uses native uni execution and starts no model subprocess."
  ],
